 "notes": [
  "Price crossing up the default SAR on 1h gave 6,663 entries in 4,071 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0.06% ahead of random entries, inside a luck band of -0.06% to 0.07%. On 4h the same cross lands at -0.01%. On daily it lands at 0.37%, inside a band of -1.68% to 1.68%.",
  "The short on a cross down through the SAR is the only default setting that left the band, and only barely. On 1h it came out 0.07% ahead after 20 candles, against a band top of 0.05%, and it was chance at 10, 50 and 100 candles. On BTC alone the result came from signals on Jun 10–12, 2022, around the Celsius withdrawal freeze, and without them it was chance. On 4h it was -0.18% and on daily -1.53%, both inside their bands.",
  "The level settings enter on almost every candle, so they behave like a coin flip on trend. Price above the SAR on 1h gave 82,394 entries but only 1,002 separate moves, with a result of 0.01% against a band of -0.07% to 0.04%. Price below the SAR, short, also came out at 0.01%. On daily each coin has fewer than 30 moves, too few to judge, and SOL's 3.07% above the SAR came from one stretch of 276 entries between Dec 28, 2020 and Apr 24, 2022.",
  "Slowing the SAR to Start 0.01, Increment 0.01 cuts the crosses: on 1h it gave 4,018 upward crosses against 6,663 for the default. Pooled, the slower cross came out at 0.05%, inside the band. On SOL 1h it reached 0.24% against a band of -0.2% to 0.2%, held without its strongest episode on Sep 9, 2020, and was still above the band at 50 and 100 candles. At 10 candles it was chance, and on BTC and ETH it was -0.07% and -0.04%.",
  "Single stretches can fake a result. Shorting a daily cross down through the SAR on ETH looked worse than random, at -2.88% against a band floor of -2.33%. That came from 3 entries between Jun 30, 2022 and Jul 26, 2022, and without them it was chance.",
  "For a long or short DCA bot on these pairs, a SAR flip as a start condition does not change where price went 20 candles later, so the take profit and DCA orders do the work. If you test it, use the slower SAR on SOL 1h as a filter beside your other conditions, and give deals room: it showed at 50 and 100 candles but not at 10, so a tight take profit closes before the move it caught. On BTC and ETH, leaving the SAR out costs nothing in this data."
